# data/records/ and data/records_merged/ are DELIBERATELY TRACKED since 2026-09-13.
# They are the evidence for every published figure -- F1 0.510 and 0.665, the
# per-document table, the reviewer's acceptance bands, score_report.json -- and
# extraction is NOT deterministic, so re-running does not recover them. Untracked,
# those numbers were reproducible on one machine and nowhere else.
# THE TRADE: a new extraction run now dirties the tree. That is deliberate. These
# are tracked evidence, not disposable build output, and a dirty status after a run
# is the correct signal that the evidence has moved.
data/advisories/
data/repeats/
data/reviewed/
data/records_extraction_only/
data/proposals.jsonl
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Slice 2: a feeds run's working folder (listings, fetched documents, items.json). Never tracked;
# a run's results enter tracked data only through tools/accept_run.py.
inbox/

# Slice 2 B: the triage back-catalogue's pinned documents and listings (hashes in evals/feeds/catalogue.json),
# and the eval runner's resume state. Never tracked.
evals/feeds/docs/
evals/feeds/repeats/.progress/
